Manage the observe dashboard's user accounts.

  Users sign in to the dashboard, or with `nexora login`, using a username and
  password. A correct password mints a user API key that is valid for 12 hours
  and is recorded under the user's name in the audit log.

  Passwords are never stored: each is hashed with PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (600,000
  iterations, random salt) into ~/.nexora/observe-users, which only you can
  read. Passwords must be 12 to 128 characters and differ from the username.

  Changes reach a running `nexora observe` immediately; no restart is needed.
  Removing a user or changing a password ends their sessions and keys.

  Subcommands
  ───────────
    add <username>       Create a user (prompts for the password twice)
    passwd <username>    Change a password
    remove <username>    Delete a user
    list                 List users

  Examples
  ────────
  Add a user interactively:
    nexora user add alice

  Add a user from a script (password on the first line of stdin):
    printf '%s\n' "$ALICE_PASSWORD" | nexora user add alice --password-stdin

  Use a non-default file (must match `nexora observe --users-file`):
    nexora user list --users-file /etc/nexora/users
